      "content": "Even at a \"standard\" dose, Vitamin K can interfere with warfarin enough to cause dangerous fluctuations in your blood clotting levels, invalidating the need for such strict caution. Your doctor likely understands the risk and prescribed a controlled amount, but you must monitor your blood tests very closely to ensure they remain in the therapeutic range. Never adjust or initiate new vitamin supplements while on warfarin without real-time monitoring from your healthcare provider, as bone health can often be maintained through diet alone or alternative treatments that do not conflict with your medication.",
